  "settingsResetScheduleSharingFailed": "Your schedule was reset, but your old shared schedule may still be visible. When the app is working again, go to Schedule Sharing → Share My Schedule → Stop Sharing.",
  "settingsResetScheduleConfirm": "Reset your shift schedule and all alarms?\n\nAll team schedules, alarm history and creation records will also be deleted. Sharing your schedule will stop too. If offline, sharing stops after reconnecting; the previously shared schedule may remain visible until then.",
  "privacyIntro": "Your shift and alarm data is stored on your device. ShiftBell also uses Google services for usage statistics and advertising. This policy explains those services, local files and data retained from features used before switching to English.",
  "privacyNoCollectionTitle": "Data stored on your device",
  "privacyNoCollectionBody": "Your shifts, alarm settings and history, notes, work hours and overtime are stored in the app’s local database. These contents are not included in analytics events or advertising requests.\n\nThe Events tab, sleep tracking and schedule sharing are unavailable in English. Switching languages does not erase records you created while using those features in Korean. They may remain in the database and in backups. Automatic sleep estimation is disabled in English.\n\nOn Android 10 or later, diagnostic files are saved locally in Download/ShiftBell/log. They include device and Android versions, permission and battery settings, and alarm and backup processing records. Note or event contents, shift names and friend names are excluded. The app does not send these files automatically.",
  "privacyAnalyticsTitle": "Usage statistics (Google Firebase Analytics)",
  "privacyAnalyticsBody": "Google Firebase Analytics collects usage and device information, such as app opens, screen views, app and operating-system versions, device model, approximate region and an installation identifier. ShiftBell also records feature-use events, such as dismissing or snoozing an alarm, saving a note or creating a backup.\n\nThese events do not include shift names, alarm times, note text or other schedule contents. Statistics are processed under Google’s privacy policy.",
  "privacyFirebaseTitle": "Google services and previous sharing",
  "privacyFirebaseBody": "Sharing is unavailable in English. If sharing was enabled before switching languages, ShiftBell stops new uploads and requests deletion of the previously shared schedule. If the device is offline, deletion is retried when the app can connect. Until the server confirms deletion, an old link may still show the previously shared schedule. Copies or screenshots held by other people cannot be recalled.\n\nPreviously shared data consists of the display name, shift pattern, start date, shift colors and date-specific shift changes. It does not include notes, overtime, alarm settings or sleep records. Sharing uses an anonymous Firebase identifier. Reinstalling can make data associated with a previous identifier inaccessible from the app.\n\nUpdate availability is checked through Google Play. Korean holiday updates use a public Firebase document when the app is in Korean; no shift or note contents are sent with that request.",
  "privacyAdsTitle": "Advertising (Google AdMob)",
  "privacyAdsBody": "ShiftBell displays Google AdMob banner ads. The advertising SDK may process device identifiers, IP addresses, app interactions and diagnostics to provide and measure ads. ShiftBell does not include your shift schedule, alarm times or note contents in ad requests.\n\nWhere required by Google’s consent system, the app asks for your advertising choices. When available, use Ad Privacy Settings in Settings to review them. Google’s privacy policy describes how Google handles this information.",
  "privacyPermissionsTitle": "Permissions the app requests",
  "privacyPermissionsBody": "• Notifications: show alarm status and pre-alarm reminders.\n• Display over other apps: show the alarm screen while you use other apps.\n• Exact alarms: schedule alarms for the time you set.\n\nYou can review these permissions in Android Settings. Declining them may limit alarm notifications or prevent alarms from working as expected.",
  "privacyDataRetentionTitle": "Data retention and deletion",
  "privacyDataRetentionBody": "Uninstalling removes the app’s local database. Backup and diagnostic files saved in Download/ShiftBell may remain; delete them with your file manager when they are no longer needed.\n\nBackups are not encrypted. They can contain your full local data, including records from features previously used in Korean. Keep them private. The app never uploads these files automatically. If you copy them to a cloud service or send them to someone, that service or recipient controls the copy.\n\nThe app keeps one manual backup and one automatic backup. A new file replaces the previous file of the same kind.\n\nPreviously shared data is handled as described in Google services and previous sharing. Google’s policies apply to retention of analytics and advertising data.",
  "privacyChildrenTitle": "Not directed at children",
  "privacyChildrenBody": "This app is not directed at children under 14, and we do not knowingly collect personal information from children.",
  "privacyContactTitle": "Contact",
  "privacyContactBody": "For app support and privacy questions:\nlowvibe07@gmail.com",
